== Fabrication and image-domain validation
<fabrication-and-image-domain-validation>
Pattern suitability is assessed from photometric agreement between the designed and captured reference pattern, residual maps between reference and lensed captures, and histogram/PSD checks over the spatial-frequency band used by optical flow.

Figure #ref(<fig:pattern_and_typical>, supplement: none) compares the digital design, the reference capture, and a distorted capture through the lens. The dashed circles mark the analysis region. The residual image (distorted minus reference) contains lens-induced deviations over several spatial scales, and the split linear/symmetric-log display makes both global variations and fine artifacts visible. The gray-level histograms stay similar apart from the darker distorted image, which is caused by attenuation through the lens. The radially averaged PSD shows that the spatial frequencies needed for optical flow remain present after fabrication and imaging.

