  caption: [
    Representative AL2550 acquisitions at nominal $0^compose$, $45^compose$, and $90^compose$ in-plane rotation states. Marker labels show tracked coded fiducials, and circles show physical-boundary detections from fixed-reference differential images. These boundary overlays are distinct from the paired fiducial-derived carrier centers used for reconstruction support.
  ]
)
<fig:supp_fiducial_rotation_states>

All measurement sets are evaluated at the same final ten-acquisition reconstruction, rather than separately optimized shapes. Figure #ref(<fig:supp_conditioning_spectrum>, supplement: none) shows the local spectra; Fig. #ref(<fig:supp_conditioning_placeholder>, supplement: none) illustrates the two optical geometries.

The Jacobian is computed by central finite differences of the weighted residual representation whose squared norm equals the component-wise L2 objective, including its 99th-percentile squared-error cap. The cap is computed before support selection and recomputed at each perturbation. Locally, $delta upright(bold(r)) approx upright(bold(J))_s delta upright(bold(s)) + upright(bold(J))_p delta upright(bold(p))$, with optimizer shape coordinates $upright(bold(s)) = \( R \, k \, A_(4 \, n) \, A_(6 \, n) \, A_(8 \, n) \)$ and per-acquisition pose coordinates $upright(bold(p)) = \( t_x \, t_y \, r_x \, r_y \)$. Physical polynomial scales are $10^(- 5)$, $10^(- 9)$, and $10^(- 12)$ for $A_4 \, A_6 \, A_8$. Eliminating the linearized pose increment gives the Schur complement @Triggs2000BundleAdjustment $ upright(bold(H))_(upright(s h a p e)) = upright(bold(J))_s^(sans(T)) upright(bold(J))_s - upright(bold(J))_s^(sans(T)) upright(bold(J))_p (upright(bold(J))_p^(sans(T)) upright(bold(J))_p)^(+) upright(bold(J))_p^(sans(T)) upright(bold(J))_s \, $<eq:supp_profiled_shape_information> where $\( dot.op \)^(+)$ is the Moore--Penrose pseudoinverse @Penrose1955GeneralizedInverse, using relative cutoff $10^(- 12)$. This accounts for local pose adjustments and is related to projection in separable least squares @GolubPereyra1973\; it is a post-reconstruction diagnostic, not exact optimization over nonlinear poses. Summing the objective-weighted acquisition blocks gives the averaged objective normal matrix. Multiplication by the total acquisition weight gives the reported information sum and preserves condition numbers. We report the normal-matrix positive-spectrum ratio $ kappa = lambda_max / lambda_min^(+) \, $ with relative eigenvalue cutoff $10^(- 12)$. The values apply to the stated fixed coordinates; for full rank, this normal-matrix ratio is the square of the effective Jacobian condition number. Each plotted spectrum is divided by its largest eigenvalue, showing relative conditioning rather than absolute sensitivity.

All tested sets retain numerical rank five at this cutoff and remain strongly ill-conditioned. The condition numbers are $5.1 times 10^10$ for one baseline acquisition, $6.6 times 10^10$ for three baseline rotations, $6.2 times 10^10$ after adding nominal-zero reseats, $5.0 times 10^10$ for matched baseline and slab-assisted rotations, and $4.9 times 10^10$ for all ten acquisitions. The slab modestly improves relative conditioning without resolving coefficient correlation. Added measurements can increase absolute information even when the condition number worsens. These local results are conditional on the fixed calibration, thickness, index, rear surface, plate model, and scoring support; they establish neither global uniqueness nor measurement uncertainty.

