    Ray-tracing recovery of a 4-cycles-per-aperture, $0.25 thin mu upright(m)$-RMS directional sinusoidal sag perturbation. Left: injected sag. Center: recovered sag using the 16-mode sinusoidal basis with acquisition-pose increments fitted simultaneously in the linearized inverse. Right: recovered minus injected sag, shown in nanometers. The recovery-error RMS over the full displayed aperture is $0.065 thin upright(n m)$ (normalized RMS error $2.6 times 10^(- 4)$). Image formation and optical-flow estimation are not included in this test.
  ]
